<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murska Sobota</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Murska Sobota is the main town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prekmurje">Prekmurje</a>, the region beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mur-river">Mura</a> river in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a>, which belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> until 1919. On 29 May 1919, amid the turmoil of the Hungarian Soviet Republic, the local politician <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilmos-tkalecz">Vilmos Tkálecz</a> proclaimed the short-lived Mura Republic there. The region passed to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a> later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/murska-sobota.jpg" alt="Murska Sobota" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sl-Ziga · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MurskaSobota1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
